    "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#semantics-2 already says\r\n\r\n> Authors must not use elements, attributes, or attribute values for purposes other than their appropriate intended semantic purpose, as doing so prevents software from correctly processing the page.\r\n\r\nSaying that a particular element is \"last resort\" serves to discourage its use, but it's not clear to me what the upside is to discourage using the `b` element.\r\n\r\nThe `i` element has similar text, but without \"should\":\r\n\r\n> Authors are encouraged to consider whether other elements might be more applicable than the [i](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-i-element) element, for instance the [em](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-em-element) element for marking up stress emphasis, or the [dfn](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-dfn-element) element to mark up the defining instance of a term.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
